  "response": "\nWhen running the code segment, the following values will be displayed:\n\n* `print(r)`: Output will be `1`\n* `print(s)`: Output will be `2`\n\nThis is because the variables `r`, `s`, and `t` are mutating each other's values. The line `r \u2190 s` assigns the value of `s` to `r`, which means that `r` now holds the value `2`. Then, in the next line, `s \u2190 t` assigns the value of `t` to `s`, which means that `s` now holds the value `3`.\n\nSo, when you print the values of `r` and `s`, you will see the following output:\n\n* `print(r)`: Output will be `2`\n* `print(s)`: Output will be `3`",
